speechtext:
Section 2, subparagraph (1) <a) reads:
a joint loan shall be made only to the person (in this section called the "home owner") who owns the land or is a lessee thereof under a long-term lease, and intends to occupy the house or one of the family housing units thereof, or to a builder who intends to sell the house to a person (in this section called the "home purchaser") who will own and occupy the house or one of the family housing units thereof;
When these joint loans are made to the builder who is building to sell, what control is there over that money?
